{"message":"I appreciate that perspective, but popular consensus doesn't make an assessment inherently right. People often focus on the immediate conveniences—staying in touch, sharing news, finding niche communities—which are real benefits. 

However, looking at the systemic level, the business models designed around outrage algorithms, engagement at the cost of mental health, and the erosion of civic discourse point toward a serious net negative. I've considered the counterarguments, but I stand by my view. 

What makes your colleagues and researchers so confident it's been a net positive, despite all the measurable downsides?"}
